[?2004l[?2004huser@c9da50e81b0b:~/infra-configs$ cat > SECURITY.md << 'EOF'
[?2004l[?2004h> # Security Measures for infra-configs Repository
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ## Git Hooks Protection
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> This repository contains sensitive private keys and has multiple layers of protection:
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ### 1. Pre-commit Hook
[?2004l[?2004h> - Checks staged files matching `*.pem` or `*.key` for insecure permissions
[?2004l[?2004h> - Blocks commits where private keys have permissions other than 0600 or 0400
[?2004l[?2004h> - **WARNING**: Can be bypassed with `git commit --no-verify` (DO NOT USE)
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ### 2. Pre-push Hook  
[?2004l[?2004h> - Scans all commits being pushed for insecure private key permissions
[?2004l[?2004h> - Checks the actual file mode stored in git (not just filesystem permissions)
[?2004l[?2004h> - Provides a second line of defense if pre-commit was bypassed
[?2004l[?2004h> - Cannot be bypassed as easily as pre-commit
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ### 3. Pre-receive Hook
[?2004l[?2004h> - Server-side validation (for bare/remote repositories)
[?2004l[?2004h> - Final enforcement point that cannot be bypassed by clients
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ## How the Previous Breach Occurred
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> On commit c149e80 (3 days ago), jenkins-bot committed `secrets/deploy.key` with mode 0644 (world-readable).
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> **Root Cause**: The commit was made using `git commit --no-verify` or similar, which bypassed the pre-commit hook.
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ## Prevention Measures Now in Place
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> 1. **Enhanced pre-commit hook** with clear warnings about --no-verify
[?2004l[?2004h> 2. **Pre-push hook** that catches bad commits before they reach remote
[?2004l[?2004h> 3. **Pre-receive hook** for server-side enforcement
[?2004l[?2004h> 4. **Git configuration**: `hooks.allowNoVerify = false` (advisory)
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ## Best Practices
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ### For Developers
[?2004l[?2004h> - Always use `chmod 600` on private key files before committing
[?2004l[?2004h> - Never use `--no-verify` flag with git commands
[?2004l[?2004h> - If hooks block your commit, fix the underlying issue instead of bypassing
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ### For CI/CD Systems (Jenkins, etc.)
[?2004l[?2004h> - Configure automation to respect git hooks
[?2004l[?2004h> - Never use `--no-verify` in automated scripts
[?2004l[?2004h> - Set proper file permissions before committing
[?2004l[?2004h> - Example:
[?2004l[?2004h>   ```bash
[?2004l[?2004h>   chmod 600 secrets/*.key secrets/*.pem
[?2004l[?2004h>   git add secrets/
[?2004l[?2004h>   git commit -m "update keys"  # No --no-verify!
[?2004l[?2004h>   ```
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ### For Repository Administrators
[?2004l[?2004h> - Regularly audit commit history for insecure key files:
[?2004l[?2004h>   ```bash
[?2004l[?2004h>   git log --all --pretty=format:'%H' | while read commit; do
[?2004l[?2004h>     git ls-tree -r $commit | grep -E '\.(pem|key)$' | grep -v '^100600\|^100400'
[?2004l[?2004h>   done
[?2004l[?2004h>   ```
[?2004l[?2004h> - Ensure hooks are executable: `chmod +x .git/hooks/pre-*`
[?2004l[?2004h> - For remote/bare repos, ensure hooks are installed server-side
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ## Fixing Existing Bad Commits
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> If a commit with insecure permissions is already in history:
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> 1. Fix the file permissions:
[?2004l[?2004h>    ```bash
[?2004l[?2004h>    chmod 600 secrets/deploy.key
[?2004l[?2004h>    ```
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> 2. Stage the corrected file:
[?2004l[?2004h>    ```bash
[?2004l[?2004h>    git add secrets/deploy.key
[?2004l[?2004h>    ```
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> 3. Create a new commit (preferred) or amend:
[?2004l[?2004h>    ```bash
[?2004l[?2004h>    git commit -m "fix: correct permissions on deploy.key to 0600"
[?2004l[?2004h>    ```
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> 4. Push the fix:
[?2004l[?2004h>    ```bash
[?2004l[?2004h>    git push
[?2004l[?2004h>    ```
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> **Note**: Rewriting history (git rebase/filter-branch) is generally not recommended for shared repositories unless absolutely necessary.
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ## Testing the Hooks
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> To verify hooks are working:
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ```bash
[?2004l[?2004h> # Test pre-commit
[?2004l[?2004h> touch test.key
[?2004l[?2004h> chmod 644 test.key
[?2004l[?2004h> git add test.key
[?2004l[?2004h> git commit -m "test"  # Should be blocked
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> # Cleanup
[?2004l[?2004h> git reset HEAD test.key
[?2004l[?2004h> rm test.key
[?2004l[?2004h> ```
